      "key": "descri",
      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Copy of a sketch originally used in a poster for sale of land in 1864 entitled 'View from Cheltenham, North Shore', but apparently drawn looking east from Mount Victoria, showing North Head in the background, Waitematā Harbour (right). Published in the Sun with the caption: The township of North Cheltenham, sold by auction in 1864. The T-shaped building in right foreground is where the present parish hall stands. From the auctioneer's sale plan it shows the modern Church Street and Vauxhall Road. The T shaped building at the bend was the first public building at the Flagstaff, comprising the Anglican Church and School opened 1855, when the gable end portion was erected. The other portion was added in 1860. Portion of this building is still in use as a shed. Mr. Hamilton's cottage alongside the school is still standing. In the bay under North Head may be seen the last Māori kainga at the Shore."
    },
